PR proposes to remove all the hardcoded references in combat_animation and move it in the JSONs files (environment), this will allow modders to change the combatstate graphics entirely

- adds 2 sub models to **BattleGraphicsModel**: **BattleIconsModel** and **BattleHudModel**;
- **BattleIconsModel** will include the icons, the small ones (mini tuxeball);
- **BattleHudModel** will include the hud background and tray background;
- changes `def animate_update_party_hud(self, player: NPC, home: Rect) -> None:` into `def animate_update_party_hud(self) -> None:` because player and home weren't used in the def;
- renames **battle_bg03** into **battle_interior** (default one);
- adds **animate_update_party_hud** to **combat.py** inside the def **reset_status_icons** to reflect on the mini tuxeball the change of status (from none to status or status to none); because until now it was done only during fainting or swapping;
- adds **icon** parameter to **CaptureDeviceSprite**, in this way we can pass **BattleIconsModel** and we can avoid to hardcode again the icons in **sprite.py**;
- moves all the coordinates (**layout**) in **prepare.py**;
- moves all the coordinates (**status**) in **prepare.py**, where the status icon is going to appear;
- adds two field in template (front and back path), in this way it'll be possible to remove the hardcoded components from combat_animation;
- removes `from tuxemon.states.combat.combat_menus import MainCombatMenuState` from combat.py;
- moves **empty_slot_icon** from **gfx/ui/combat/** to **gfx/ui/icons/party** where there are the icons (mini tuxeballs)
- renames **empty_slot_icon** into **party_empty**, similar to the others (eg. party_icon01, etc);

